Z||000006||JBGehling||03-26-2001||09:06 PM||||The blue GT with 1.7k miles on it was beside my indy... it looked spectacular!  I was so surprised when my indy took 1st in the stock indy class and was sort of dissapointed that I had to put my 88 GT in street custom class just because of the radio (you better believe the original's going in it next year  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!), but at least it got 5th!<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000007||RobertVol||03-26-2001||09:25 PM||||Yeah well leaving your gas cap open in Stock / Street ?? hmmmmmmm<P><BR>Oh well thanks to 87GT i will know for next year  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry I missed everyone. I did see FieroLisa's car though. NICE<P>I did see Phil and 007Doug Aka Doug Kinney<BR>and TigerFiero who is from my area. <BR>Oh yeah and Spyder! <P>Had fun!! I got a few pics of the 87Gt Blue one that only had 1700+ miles. I took a pic of the Odometer !!! I guess I was full of Envy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1">  <p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
