Z||000009||Ronnie||03-26-2001||11:54 PM||||Good looking GT Roy. I didn't get to meet many of you guys from the Forum either.We really needed a way of identifying members.I know my car is not a show car, drive mine everyday,but I did get a really good parking place!!!LOL.One thing I am proud of my car is the fact that I had the only factory leather interior there!!!! Makes me realize how rare that option must be. Had lots of fun anyway.Lots of really nice Fieros out there!! I was in Street Stock C GT class.<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd ,leather int.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero2_1_3.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000010||RobertVol||03-27-2001||12:01 AM||||What I was surprised about was there was not many T Top cars there.<P>Mine was there and I know I saw a yellow one at the Holiday inn<P>I saw Dougs 3.4 but not many more ..hmmmm||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wolfhound||03-27-2001||05:05 AM||||Roy, You really have the bubblegum blue looking good. Congrats on second place, hard to overcome 1700 mile competion.||||reg||14
Z||000012||mrfixit58||03-27-2001||09:21 AM||||Thanks for the nice comments Wolfhound (Coy),<P>Fortunatly, I wasn't compeating against the 1,800 mile GT. He was in the "Stock" group while I competed in the "Street Stock" group. What I did find interesting is when I compaired my VIN with the 1,800 mile car's VIN. His car was made only 46 cars before mine. Probably made the same week.<P>As far as fun factor goes, in the nine months I've owned my blue GT, I put twice as many miles on her then he has in 14 years! I would venture to say that I've had more fun "in" my car then he has  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> .<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
